        {
            "block_label": "figure_title",
            "block_content": "<div style=\"text-align: center;\">Figure 2: Schematic of a depth-one tbtree. The root (ellipse) fits a twoblock model under the coskewness split objective; its first  $ \\mathbf{X} $-score  $ t_1 = \\mathbf{x}_i^\\top \\mathbf{w}_1 $ orders the rows, and a threshold  $ \\tau $ routes each row to one of two leaves (rectangles). Every leaf carries its own covariance twoblock model  $ \\hat{\\mathbf{y}}_i = \\mathbf{x}_i^\\top \\mathbf{B}_\\ell $. The bar charts show, for a hypothetical six-variable predictor block, the coskewness split weights  $ \\mathbf{w}_1 $ and the two leaves' regression coefficients (blue positive, red negative), whose contrast illustrates the distinct local regimes. This figure is purely illustrative: the displayed weights and coefficients are specimen values, not fit to any dataset.</div>\n",
